# APPEND-ONLY LOGS merge by keeping BOTH sides.
#
# These files are journals: every entry is a dated record that some session
# added at the end, and two sessions appending on the same day conflict every
# single time even though neither has touched the other's text. Resolved by
# hand three times on 2026-09-08 alone, identically each time (keep both), and
# a hand resolution on a history file is where an entry gets dropped and the
# reason a ceiling moved is lost. `union` is git's built-in driver and needs no
# configuration on a fresh clone.
#
# This is only correct BECAUSE they are append-only. Anything that rewrites
# earlier entries must not be listed here — union would keep both versions of
# the rewritten text.
docs/notes/CEILING-HISTORY.md   merge=union
